Z||000000||Fret Naught||08-02-2000||12:52 PM||||I don't think my Fiero is fast or fast enough. I have a stock V6, I can't smoke my tires when I pop the clutch the thing just launches, my buddy at work just got a 300 Z non turbo, V6, and he just walks all over me!!! I guess I just need a bigger engine<BR>in the immortal words of Tim Allen, "What this needs is MORE POWER"||||reg||9
Z||000001||1FST2M6||08-02-2000||02:47 PM||||is the clutch enguaging or slipping... are you able to chirp 2nd? is your cat plugged, you fuel filter plugged.. compression ok? ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fret Naught||08-02-2000||03:16 PM||||I chirp in second, not all the time but sometimes. I don't think the clutch is slipping. Cat is "DEFINTELY" not plugged, Compression is good 150 except #6 120, I am keeping my eye on that one. It is the rings or cylinder, not valves. Everything else seems to be kosher. I get the ocassional code 32 when running for an extended period of time above 70 MPH. ||||reg||4
Z||000003||86SE||08-02-2000||03:32 PM||||Check your air filter, fuel filter, tach filter, change your oil, try premium fuel, put some injector cleaner in it, and most importantly put some HONDA HORSEPOWER STICKERS on it!!<P>Mine is an auto and I can chirp the tires when I floor it.  It runs 0-40 before you can blink and it runs 0-112 in 1 mile.  It can go 0-100-0 in less than 1 mile too, just a 3 speed auto....but I have a big Pontiac sticker on my window and 2 Pegasus logos on the sail panels!<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||1
Z||000004||b lo 0||08-02-2000||04:22 PM||||OOH, 86 SE, I want that tire-churning power in my '85 GT Auto too-send my pics of how you installed those stickers!!  No really, something's wrong.  I don't know what, but it's there.  I can roast the meats (11 inch wide BFGs) on my '90 wrangler, with a bone stock 2.4l L4, and chirp every time in every gear but 4th and 5th.  Huh.  Must be the JEEPIN windshield banner and the RonJon's bumper sticker. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">    <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula||08-02-2000||05:05 PM||||shouldnt most of our cars do 0-100 in a mile? I thought the V6 did the 1/4 at 90+ mph?? ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Taijiguy||08-03-2000||08:43 AM||||I dunno, the 300ZX is a rocket ship. A former girlfriend had a '90, and that thing was a monster.  Now my best friend has one, same year, and it's the same thing. He can not just chirp the tires in 2nd, he can keep 'em smokin clear on up through third and sometimes into fourth! I like to think the Fiero just hooks up better. But I've always been a wee bit afraid to take him on, cause that 300 sure SEEMS quick. Anyone know the specs on power, and times of the 300?<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000007||Alex4mula||08-03-2000||09:29 AM||||It is very unfair to compare tire chirping between front engine cars and our rear engine Fiero. Put the 300 to 400 pounds of their engines in the back and you will see a very different story. You can take almost any RWD 4 cyl car of 79 & 80 (not built anymore) and chirp tires any time. No weigth in the back. A huge 2.8 80s Camaro with a bad engine can chirp tires easily too. Judge your car with race wins and 1/4 mile times but not tire chirping. Just my opinion  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||loafer87gt||08-03-2000||12:42 PM||||I checked through my ol Road n' Track collection and the 90-91 non turbo 300 Z's have 222 HP and 198 torque. The car weighs only 3200 pounds as well. It is able to do the 0-60 in 7.0 seconds and the quarter 15.4 at 91 MPH. One of my old friends used to have a 300 Z and it was a quick car, I wouldn't have stood a chance beating him with my stock v6 unless he blew a shift.||||reg||1
Z||000009||turbo86se||08-03-2000||04:54 PM||||Last summer I test drove a 93 or 94 300Z non-turbo automatic. I couldn't stand it! To me it didn't handle well, and was rather slow. My turbo 86SE would beat the he!! out of it! Insurance on that thing was almost $300 a month! No thanks!! <BR>Just my .02  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||HYPTNOTiSE||08-04-2000||09:26 AM||||my fiero bone stock ran a 16.0 at like 86mph. that was my best time when it was stock. Too slow for me too. But you have to remeber that when your car is stock, it's also more reliable! You go messing around and you run into probs like i did. I haven't driven my fiero in 6 months, been doing an engine swap. Mine will be much faster than most peoples fieros, but they also been enjoying they're slower ones, for 6 months longer that i have.<P><P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||HYPTNOTiSE||08-04-2000||09:26 AM||||my fiero bone stock ran a 16.0 at like 86mph. that was my best time when it was stock. Too slow for me too. But you have to remeber that when your car is stock, it's also more reliable! You go messing around and you run into probs like i did. I haven't driven my fiero in 6 months, been doing an engine swap. Mine will be much faster than most peoples fieros, but they also been enjoying they're slower ones, for 6 months longer that i have.<P><P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||ChadMan||08-04-2000||11:11 AM||||When I worked at Mid-Ohio as a PR intern in 1993, we had two 1993 turbo 300ZX's we used as pace cars.  One had a Stillen brake kit with drilled rotors.  Except for race weekends, we used them for regular company cars.  <P>I was pretty low on the company totem pole and usually had to drive one of our Maximas or my Fiero, but I did get the 300 with the Stillen brakes for a whole day once.  That was an absolutely bad-a$$ car - I had it up to 125 and it was still pulling hard.  I shut down a guy in what I think was a 1992 Z28 with it - he was trying and it wasn't even close.<P>I just wish the Z sounded cooler, though - the turbos muffle the exhaust quite a bit.  The leather seemed substandard, too, and the mouse-fur headliner screamed "Sentra" - way out of place on a $35K car.||||reg||1
Z||000013||N_Man||08-04-2000||03:01 PM||||Alex is right.<BR>the extra weight over our wheels makes em hook up better and go faster but harder to smoke em.<P>Im running a freshly rebuilt engine with a big cam and it still takes a bit of effort to smoke my tires||||reg||1
Z||000014||Black88GT||08-04-2000||10:24 PM||||Smoking tires is BAD for racing.  Yeah it might be good for a lame a$$ immature pissing contest, but if you pull up next to one of those ricers at a red light, they will be peeling wheels all the way to SECOND place.  I remember on motor trend TV they were saying how peeling wheels slows down the vette's qtr. mile times.  BTW, if you want to smoke a lot, put bleach on your tires (so the drag racer across the street says).  <P><BR>||||reg||1
